  "objective": "weighted_BCE + .1*(paired_CTC_NLL_per_token + background_gain*mean_background_blank_NLL_per_frame). Both arms keep paired CTC gain.1; additional background gain0 versus1. Empty compact target has the unique all-blank path. This target means no compact wake/confuser phrase in the already labeled ambient cohort, not acoustic silence or an actual phone transcript. Separate mean reductions preserve paired-example and token normalization. Zero gain does not add a zero-valued tensor to the old loss graph.",
  "warmup_policy": "Exactly replay parent compact-CTC1000-step warmup. Both arms have the same cached frozen encoder states, head weights, schedule and unchanged binary weights/optimizer before joint training.",
  "limits": "Reused development validation and unchanged21-point grid/gates. Existing training-only ambient negatives receive an extra compact task label without a transcript; their original binary role is unchanged. Byte and metadata disjointness does not prove semantic labels, absence of partial overlaps or independent split design. Synthesis intent is not pronunciation truth. Auxiliary head discarded from scalar export. No final/test inference, threshold extension, validation-residual fitting, audio playback, microphone capture, board/OTA, production device, PCM speed or audio pipeline change. Real-speaker recall, physical latency, P4 resources and call stability remain unproven.",
  "study_boundary": "Freeze before training. Retrain both arms on identical actual bytes and random schedules. Reuse the parent compact-CTC development cache as new control only after exact scalar INT8 export, legacy first16 batch prefix, full PTQ input, complete warmup and pair schedule replay. If replay fails, stop without comparing or silently falling back. Fresh treatment validation only; retain full traces and independently reconstruct them.",
